{"shortDescription":"Restaurant stocks are on the defensive Tuesday as industry data showed a meaningful decline in dining traffic, albeit largely driven by the timing of this year’s Labor Day weekend.According to the  August 2026 Retail and Dining Index from Placer.ai, dining visits were down 2.4% in August, reversing…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Restaurant stocks are on the defensive Tuesday as industry data showed a meaningful decline in dining traffic, albeit largely driven by the timing of this year’s Labor Day weekend."]},{"type":"p","children":["According to the  August 2026 Retail and Dining Index from Placer.ai, dining visits were down 2.4% in August, reversing a gradual improvement in June and July after a 2.5% decline in May 2026."]},{"type":"p","children":["Because of the timing of the Labor Day weekend this year, dining activity that would typically begin in late August was pushed into September with the Labor Day holiday falling on September 7 vs. September 1 in 2025."]},{"type":"p","children":["The survey also attributes the soft dining trends to macroeconomic conditions, as a gallon of gas exceeded $4 per gallon in August, putting 2026 on track as one of the most expensive years for gas."]},{"type":"p","children":["Dining traffic was down in every state except California, which saw a slight uptick from a year ago. Notable weakness was seen in Montana, Wyoming, South Dakota, New Mexico, Vermont, and West Virginia."]},{"type":"p","children":["The pressure on the restaurant sector is weighing on the Consumer Discretionary SPDR ETF ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"AMEX:XLY","text":"AMEX:XLY"}}," and Vanguard Consumer Discretionary ETF ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"AMEX:VCR","text":"AMEX:VCR"}},"."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Related tickers: "]},"Black Rock Coffee ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:BRCB","text":"NASDAQ:BRCB"}},", Wingstop ",{"type":"symbol","params